        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Lhasa</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">637 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songtsen-gampo">Songtsen Gampo</a> moved the capital of the Tibetan Empire to Rasa (Lhasa) and in 637 raised the first structures on the site of the present <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potala-palace">Potala Palace</a>; he built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jokhang">Jokhang</a> and Ramoche temples in 641.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the middle reaches of the Lhasa (Kyi) River, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarlung-tsangpo">Yarlung Zangbo</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a>), at about 3,650 metres on the Tibetan Plateau, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> Autonomous Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</span></div>
